  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-09-02T22:44:19.869Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Description\nSeems like one of the last updates caused a change in how the eye movement is handled. If you're using different transform chains for eyes, your right eye's transform chain will follow that of the left eye's, causing it to copy rotations (and apply animated rotations) to the transform that is now misaligned from its parent.\nOnly tested with humanoids, so the results may not cover generics.\nReplication\n1. Use a humanoid model with eye bones parented to the head (humanoid eye setup is not required)\n2. Create an empty object as direct child of the prefab\n3. Assign newly created object as a left eye transform\n4. Assign right eye normally\n5. Upload the avatar\n6. Tilt the head at runtime: you should notice the right eye keeping rotations of the object referenced in the left eye slot instead of rotating with the head",
  "error": null,
